{
    "_comment": "Tunable boundary parameters for every model type (A-F, S). 'x_max'/'z_max' are resolved to the model's actual length/depth at runtime; any field can instead be a fixed number.",
    "_legend": {
        "amplitude": "Wave height of the sine/cosine boundary (peak-to-peak), in the same units as z_max/depth.",
        "period": "Wavelength of the sine/cosine boundary along x, in the same units as x_max/length. Smaller value = more oscillations.",
        "phase_shift": "Horizontal offset (along x) that shifts where the wave starts.",
        "vertical_shift": "Vertical offset (depth) the wave is centered around.",
        "low": "Minimum value the Beta-PERT distribution can sample for this parameter.",
        "peak": "Most likely value (the distribution's mode) for this parameter.",
        "high": "Maximum value the Beta-PERT distribution can sample for this parameter.",
        "lamb": "Beta-PERT shape parameter: how tightly sampled values cluster around 'peak'. Higher = more concentrated near peak, lower = flatter/more spread out. Defaults to 10 if omitted.",
        "bands": "List of [start_depth, end_depth] pairs (z_max units) marking where each layer boundary sits, used by the banded/vertical layering models (B, D).",
        "functions": "Which wave shapes ('sin' and/or 'cos') may be randomly picked for the boundary.",
        "x_max/z_max as string values": "Placeholders meaning 'use the model's actual length (x_max) or depth (z_max) at runtime' instead of a fixed number."
